Kept so that a fresh clone compiles.

`//go:embed all:web/dist` in main.go is resolved by the compiler, not at run
time, and it fails the build when the directory does not exist. Git does not
track directories, only files, so without something in here the first thing a
new clone does is fail at `go build` with a message about a missing pattern
rather than about a missing build step.

What to serve when nothing has been built is placeholder.html, which lives
outside this directory where a build cannot overwrite it.
